Subject: [PATCH] ion: a camera heap of system memory

Since Android 8, the usage bit that this platform's gralloc reads as "allocate from
the camera heap" (GRALLOC_USAGE_PRIVATE_CAMERA_HEAP, 0x00400000) is
BufferUsage::VIDEO_DECODER to the framework, which sets it on every output buffer of
a hardware video decoder. This tablet's heaps are system, system-contig, secure,
qseecom and audio, with no camera heap (ION_CAMERA_HEAP_ID, 20), so each such
allocation failed with "No such device" and the decoder stopped before its first
frame: VP9 video in the browser stayed still with no sound.

Heap 20 is now declared as one more system heap, as heap 25 is, so a buffer asked
from it is plain paged memory. That is what the decoder got before, when LineageOS 20
changed gralloc instead so that the bit no longer named a heap, and played VP9 with
it; with this the platform's gralloc is used as it is.
---
--- arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/msm8976-ion.dtsi
+++ arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/msm8976-ion.dtsi
@@ -21,6 +21,15 @@
 			qcom,ion-heap-type = "SYSTEM";
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * The camera heap, as plain system memory: Android asks for it for the
+		 * buffers of hardware video decoders, and fails with no such heap.
+		 */
+		qcom,ion-heap@20 {
+			reg = <20>;
+			qcom,ion-heap-type = "SYSTEM";
+		};
+
 		qcom,ion-heap@21 {
 			reg = <21>;
 			qcom,ion-heap-type = "SYSTEM_CONTIG";
